{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "cwMXL39eC2", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761279, "segment_id": "uvYOZZVAmj", "segment_broadcast_id": "cwMXL39eC2", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction John Roberts (New York)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 40, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761279, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "cwMXL39eC2", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761279, "segment_id": "Vo9Sc38Spd", "segment_broadcast_id": "cwMXL39eC2", "segment_title": "Terrorism / Al Qaeda Threat / Talha Capture", "segment_description": "(Studio: John Roberts) Report introduced. \n (Washington: Bob Orr) Heightened security in response to an Al Qaeda threat targeting specific buildings featured; scenes shown from New York\u2019s Citigroup complex, the New York Stock Exchange, the Prudential Financial building in Newark, New Jersey, and the subway in Washington, DC; map shown of the five targeted sites; details given about what was learned from an Al Qaeda suspect arrested in Pakistan; terrorist document quoted. [Center for Strategic & International Studies David HEYMAN&#134;- explains the difficulty in identifying terrorist agents.] \n (Studio: John Roberts) Report introduced. \n (Pentagon: David Martin) The capture in Pakistan of Al Qaeda operative Abu Talha&#134; {aka Mohammed Khan&#134;&#134;}, whose computer yielded the information about the surveillance of US financial institutions, featured; details given of the importance of the assistance of Pakistani President Pervez Musharraf.", "segment_duration": 270, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63040.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761280, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "cwMXL39eC2", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761279, "segment_id": "36WJWE010L", "segment_broadcast_id": "cwMXL39eC2", "segment_title": "September 11 / Commission Report / Political Impact", "segment_description": "(Studio: John Roberts) Report introduced. \n (White House: Thalia Assuras) President Bush\u2019s endorsement of the 9/11 Commission\u2019s main recommendations, the creation of a national intelligence director and the establishment of a national counterterrorism center, featured. [BUSH \u2013 says we are a nation in danger; states the intelligence director should be a stand-alone group.] [9/11 Commission Timothy ROEMER&#134;- notes the importance in Washington of power over the budget and power to hire & fire.] [White House chief of staff Andrew CARD&#134;- says the president has made a decision that allows for the intelligence director to have clout.] The political implications of Bush\u2019s move noted. \n (Grand Rapids, Michigan: Jim Axelrod) The impact on the campaign of Senator John Kerry of the new terror alert featured; details given of Kerry\u2019s shift in his message from jobs to terror; CBS News poll results cited. [In Michigan, KERRY \u2013 criticizes Bush for not acting sooner; calls for Congress to interrupt its recess to implement the 9/11 Commission\u2019s recommendations; blames the administration for increases in anger towards the US and terrorist recruitment.] \n (Studio: John Roberts) The views of National Security Advisor Condoleezza Rice on the creation of a national intelligence director and on the current terror threat presented. [RICE \u2013 explains why Bush believes the appointee should be separate from the White House; says we are working to disrupt any plots that might be underway.]", "segment_duration": 340, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63310.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761281, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "cwMXL39eC2", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761279, "segment_id": "5t3zoLVTlz", "segment_broadcast_id": "cwMXL39eC2", "segment_title": "Iraq / Unrest", "segment_description": "(Studio: John Roberts) A gun battle in Najaf, Iraq, involving US Marines, and a video showing militants killing a Turkish hostage noted.", "segment_duration": 30, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63650.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761282, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "cwMXL39eC2", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761279, "segment_id": "e9NgH0LiN0", "segment_broadcast_id": "cwMXL39eC2", "segment_title": "Upcoming Items; fallen soldier Army Cpl. John T. Rivero&#134<!-- spelling on screen --> profiled. (Studio: John Roberts, Dan Rather)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 50, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63680.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761283, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "cwMXL39eC2", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761279, "segment_id": "V0sikBXYJN", "segment_broadcast_id": "cwMXL39eC2", "segment_title": "(Commercial: Viactiv; Covergirl; Detrol; Benefiber; Centrum; Total.)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 160, "segment_type_id": 3, "segment_start_time": "63730.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761284, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Commercial", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "cwMXL39eC2", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761279, "segment_id": "W8wFQm70oi", "segment_broadcast_id": "cwMXL39eC2", "segment_title": "Market Watch: Oil Prices, Stocks", "segment_description": "(Studio: John Roberts) Crude oil prices cited; Stock Market Report.", "segment_duration": 10, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63890.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761285, "network_name": "